<title>NETHERLANDS: Gas boss urges removing states' roles in EU market.</title>
<headline>Gas boss urges removing states' roles in EU market.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The liberalisation of Europe's gas market will only succeed if it creates a level playing field out of reach of national and European legislators, the president of Mobil Gas Europe said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The greatest initial contribution the EU can make is to remove the state monopolies and exclusive rights for imports, exports, sales and transportation which still exist in some member states,&quot; Dr Axel Commichau told an audience of industry chiefs at the European Gas 97 conference.</p>
<p>He added public service and regulatory arguments put forward by certain parties in support of limited liberalisation were &quot;simply attempts to allow monopoly positions to be maintained&quot;.</p>
<p>He urged the European Union not to produce a simple copy of its Electricity Directive, saying a Gas Directive required &quot;a tailor-made approach, not a carbon copy&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
